CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ body pack-expansion call expanded to full arity: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*wrong number of function arguments.*$
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5: a pack-expansion use of a function parameter pack in a
function body (here `fp(a...)`, with `a` the parameter pack of `go(A... a)` and
`A` the enclosing class template parameter pack) must expand to one argument per
deduced element.  This is the libstdc++
function<_Res(_ArgTypes...)>::operator() body shape
`_M_invoker(_M_functor, std::forward<_ArgTypes>(__args)...)`.

Fixed: when template_mapt expands a member's parameter pack during
instantiation of a partial-specialization class C<R(A...)>, the replicated
parameters are now given distinct names base$k (template_mapt::
expand_parameter_packs), and cpp_typecheck_method_bodies recovers the per-pack
counts from those names when no in-class #expanded_param_packs record exists, so
the body pack-expansion uses expand to the full deduced arity.  Non-vacuous
(assertion 2 must FAIL).
